          your WebP files into the converter at once, and download them all as JPGs individually or as
          a ZIP file. This is especially useful for web designers, photographers, and anyone who
          regularly works with WebP images from downloads or exports.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a dedicated batch conversion workflow, try our <a href="/tools/image-compressor">Image
          Compressor</a> which supports multiple file processing with quality control. You can also
          use our <a href="/webp-to-png">WebP to PNG converter</a> if you need transparency in your output.
        </p>

        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <h3>Is WebP or JPG better quality?</h3>
        <p>
          WebP and JPG can achieve similar visual quality, but WebP delivers the same quality at 25-35%
          smaller file sizes. For web publishing, WebP is better because pages load faster. For sharing,
          printing, and uploading to forms and portals, JPG is the safer choice due to its universal
          compatibility.
        </p>

        <h3>Does converting WebP to JPG lose quality?</h3>
        <p>
          Converting WebP to JPG involves re-encoding the image, which can introduce minor quality loss.
          However, using a high-quality converter like QuickJPG minimizes this loss. For most use cases —
          social media, forms, email — the difference is imperceptible. Always keep your original WebP
          files if you need lossless access later.
        </p>

        <h3>Can I convert WebP to JPG on iPhone?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. Open Safari and go to <a href="/webp-to-jpg">QuickJPG's WebP to JPG converter</a>.
          Upload your WebP file, tap convert, and download the JPG. The entire process happens in your
          browser — no app installation needed. You can also use the Shortcuts app to create an
          automation for batch conversion.
        </p>

        <h3>Is the QuickJPG WebP converter free?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes, QuickJPG is 100% free with no limits. You can convert unlimited WebP files to JPG without
          creating an account, and there are no watermarks or restrictions. All processing happens in
          your browser for complete privacy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-brand-50 dark:bg-brand-950/30 border border-brand-200 dark:border-brand-800 text-center">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary mb-2">Convert Your WebP Files Now</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">Free, instant, and private. No signup required.</p>
        <a href="/webp-to-jpg" class="btn-primary">Convert WebP to JPG →</a>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
